/* THE JOIN, LITERALLY — identity match, not count correlation.

   06_remediation_effectiveness.ppl shows 104 incidents still erroring after
   the agent reported success. This query proves they are THE SAME incidents
   whose rollback silently ran twice — by joining the agent's root spans to
   the platform's own error stream on run_id = incident_id. One query, one
   cluster: the sentence "joining agent traces to the platform's own logs"
   executed as written. An agent-observability island cannot run this,
   because it holds only the left side.

   Expected: 104 rows · every row errors_after = 8 · every row had
   tool_retries > 0 by construction of the left side.

   PPL `join` ships in OpenSearch 3.x — verified working on this stack
   (3.7.0, stock image, no settings changed).                              */
source = otel-v1-apm-span-*
| where name = 'incident.remediate' and `span.attributes.agent@release` = '2026.09.1'
| where `span.attributes.agent@tool_retries` > 0
| join ON `span.attributes.agent@run_id` = incident_id
  [
    source = platform-logs
    | where level = 'ERROR' and phase = 'post_remediation'
    | stats count() as errors_after by incident_id
  ]
| fields `span.attributes.agent@run_id`, errors_after
| sort `span.attributes.agent@run_id`
